# ── Build context exclusions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prevents 7+ GB of gameplay footage and dev artefacts from being sent to the
# Docker daemon on every build. The Dockerfile only COPYs what it needs.

# Gameplay source videos (NEVER bake into image — too large, use runtime mount or R2)
storage/gameplay/*.mp4
storage/gameplay/*.webm
# Keep the _small.mp4 previews that ARE committed to git and used at runtime
!storage/gameplay/*_small.mp4

# Generated outputs and temp files (ephemeral, not needed in image)
storage/outputs/
storage/output/
storage/temp/
storage/audio/
storage/subtitles/

# Runtime stores — must never be baked into an image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY storage/ ./storage/`, so anything not excluded here is
# captured into an image layer. That included storage/userStore.json (every
# customer's email, plan and Stripe customer/subscription id) and
# storage/jobStore.json (every submitted story) — a developer's local copy would
# ship to the registry inside the image, where it survives even if the file is
# later deleted. Image layers are not scrubbable by a redeploy.
#
# Note: these are single-star patterns on purpose. Docker matches with
# filepath.Match, so `**` is NOT a globstar here — `storage/**/*.json` silently
# matches nothing at all, which is exactly the failure this file exists to prevent.
storage/*.json
storage/*.corrupt-*
storage/*.tmp

# Node modules (rebuilt in Docker via npm ci)
node_modules/

# Dev / OS files
.env
.git/
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak

# Root-level test & scratch files
/*.mp4
/*.mp3
/*.png
tts_test.*
test_*
test-*
generate_*.js
upload.js
bgsample1.png
.kilo/

# ── Dead frontend media ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY frontend/ ./frontend/`, so every byte here lands in an
# image layer. frontend/ currently carries ~385 MB of files that NOTHING
# references — verified by grepping every .html/.js/.css in frontend/ for each
# filename. They are git-tracked (so still recoverable from history) but they were
# being uploaded to the daemon and pushed into the registry on every build.
#
#   frontend/*_small.mp4              287 MB  gameplay.service.js resolves these
#                                             under storage/gameplay/, NOT
#                                             frontend/ — the frontend copies are
#                                             shadow duplicates
#   frontend/example_1..4.mp4          71 MB  the pages all load media/example_*.mp4
#   frontend/hero-mid.png, bgsample1.png,
#   card-left.jpg, card-right.jpg,
#   bg-signin.jpg, 8x UUID .png        28 MB  unreferenced
#
# Deleting them is a separate decision (see AGENT_LOG.md); excluding them from the
# build context is free and takes effect immediately.
frontend/*_small.mp4
frontend/example_*.mp4
frontend/hero-mid.png
frontend/bgsample1.png
frontend/card-left.jpg
frontend/card-right.jpg
frontend/bg-signin.jpg
frontend/bg-minecraft.png
frontend/card-media/card-cod.jpg
frontend/card-media/card-valorant.jpg
frontend/[0-9a-f]*-[0-9a-f]*-[0-9a-f]*-[0-9a-f]*-[0-9a-f]*.png
